<title>SYRIA: Syria opens 80,000 cubic metres per day gas plant.</title>
<headline>Syria opens 80,000 cubic metres per day gas plant.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria on Thursday opened a plant producing 80,000 cubic metres of gas per day for nearby power stations.</p>
<p>Official sources said Oil Minister Mohamed Maher Jamal opened the Jafra plant in northeastern Syria near the city of Deir ez-Zor.</p>
<p>Syria, which produces around 600,000 barrels of oil per day, is planning to increase its gas production capacity to 16.05 million cubic metres per day in the year 2000 from 8.05 million produced in 1995.</p>
<p>The increase is needed to cover booming gas demand from power plants and new industrial projects.</p>
</text>
